{
  "type": "music",
  "id": "names",
  "version": 1,
  "note": "How the composer names a piece it grows (doc 24, Naming). The same seed, season and slot always give the same name, so a name can be shown, remembered and found again. templates: one is drawn per piece; {key} is filled from the word lists, each word used at most once in a name. Lists merge from common, the season and the slot (the season's and slot's words are drawn twice as often, so names lean seasonal). one: singular things, for 'The {one} {verb}'; many: plural or mass things; verb: present tense for a singular subject. Edit or swap any list freely: names change, nothing else does. Authored pieces keep their own titles. Words are checked against avoid before use.",
  "templates": [
    "{adj} {many}",
    "{many} {prep} {place}",
    "{many} and {many}",
    "The {one} {verb}",
    "{many} at {when}",
    "{adj} {one}",
    "Song for {a} {one}"
  ],
